                label = "Horde: Frostwall Town Hall - follower table; position varies by garrison level",
            },
            { mapID = 107, x = 0.33, y = 0.46, step = 4, label = "Optional: Sunspring Post - Crystal Powder farming" },
            { mapID = 107, x = 0.428, y = 0.425, step = 4, label = "Halaa - optional PvP tokens and powder exchanges" },
            { mapID = 107, x = 0.428, y = 0.425, step = 5, label = "Halaa - capture the town if necessary" },
            { mapID = 107, x = 0.428, y = 0.425, step = 6, label = "Aldraan / Coreiel - buy the selected dark talbuk" },
        },
        itemId = 29228,
        name = "Dark War Talbuk",
        stepCount = 7,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Obtain Halaa tokens through contested PvP or an unpredictable garrison mission, then control Halaa to buy the mount.\n\n1. Choose how to collect 100 Halaa Battle Tokens and 20 Halaa Research Tokens for Dark War Talbuk. No Kurenai or Mag'har Exalted reputation is required. If collecting both dark talbuks, budget 170 Battle and 35 Research Tokens in total.\n\n2. For the route without token farming in PvP, use your Draenor Garrison Hearthstone and check the follower Command Table in your Town Hall: Lunarfall for Alliance or Frostwall for Horde. Look for the rare mission Mysteries of Lok-rath (332). Level and equip your Draenor followers through ordinary missions while checking back; the rare mission is random and can take a long time to appear.\n\n3. When Mysteries of Lok-rath appears, assign a follower who counters Minion Swarms and improve the success chance before sending them. It costs 10 Garrison Resources and takes 1 hour. Collect the completed reward at the table: 100 Battle and 40 Research Tokens. One success buys either mount; both require a second mission or another source of Battle Tokens.\n\n4. If you prefer the original farming alternative, earn Battle Tokens from eligible opposing-faction player kills INSIDE Halaa in Outland Nagrand. Bombing guards does not award Battle Tokens. For Research Tokens, kill Nagrand enemies for Oshu'gun Crystal Powder Samples; Sunspring Post around 33.0, 46.0 is one farming area. Exchange 10 samples per Research Token with your faction's researcher in Halaa. Skip this step if the mission supplied all your tokens.\n\n5. Bring your tokens to Halaa in OUTLAND Nagrand around 42.8, 42.5. This is not Lok-rath in Draenor. Your faction must control Halaa for its vendor to be available. If the other faction controls it, defeat its Halaani guards, then stand by the central capture flag until the capture bar finishes and your NPCs appear.\n\n6. At the northeastern part of Halaa, speak to Aldraan if Alliance controls the town or Coreiel if Horde controls it. Check the vendor's mount items, including later shop pages. Buy Reins of the Dark War Talbuk for 100 Battle Tokens plus 20 Research Tokens.\n\n7. Use the reins from your bags. Both factions can collect and use the dark talbuk appearance. Keep leftover tokens if you still need the other version; buying the cheaper Riding mount does not also unlock the armored War mount.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=29228",
        difficultyReason = "Obtain Halaa tokens through contested PvP or an unpredictable garrison mission, then control Halaa to buy the mount.",
        difficulty = "hard",
    },
