        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - Obtain Halaa tokens through contested PvP or an unpredictable garrison mission, then control Halaa to buy the mount.\n\n1. Choose how to collect 70 Halaa Battle Tokens and 15 Halaa Research Tokens for Dark Riding Talbuk. No Kurenai or Mag'har Exalted reputation is required. If collecting both dark talbuks, budget 170 Battle and 35 Research Tokens in total.\n\n2. For the route without token farming in PvP, use your Draenor Garrison Hearthstone and check the follower Command Table in your Town Hall: Lunarfall for Alliance or Frostwall for Horde. Look for the rare mission Mysteries of Lok-rath (332). Level and equip your Draenor followers through ordinary missions while checking back; the rare mission is random and can take a long time to appear.\n\n3. When Mysteries of Lok-rath appears, assign a follower who counters Minion Swarms and improve the success chance before sending them. It costs 10 Garrison Resources and takes 1 hour. Collect the completed reward at the table: 100 Battle and 40 Research Tokens. One success buys either mount; both require a second mission or another source of Battle Tokens.\n\n4. If you prefer the original farming alternative, earn Battle Tokens from eligible opposing-faction player kills INSIDE Halaa in Outland Nagrand. Bombing guards does not award Battle Tokens. For Research Tokens, kill Nagrand enemies for Oshu'gun Crystal Powder Samples; Sunspring Post around 33.0, 46.0 is one farming area. Exchange 10 samples per Research Token with your faction's researcher in Halaa. Skip this step if the mission supplied all your tokens.\n\n5. Bring your tokens to Halaa in OUTLAND Nagrand around 42.8, 42.5. This is not Lok-rath in Draenor. Your faction must control Halaa for its vendor to be available. If the other faction controls it, defeat its Halaani guards, then stand by the central capture flag until the capture bar finishes and your NPCs appear.\n\n6. At the northeastern part of Halaa, speak to Aldraan if Alliance controls the town or Coreiel if Horde controls it. Check the vendor's mount items, including later shop pages. Buy Reins of the Dark Riding Talbuk for 70 Battle Tokens plus 15 Research Tokens.\n\n7. Use the reins from your bags. Both factions can collect and use the dark talbuk appearance. Keep leftover tokens if you still need the other version; buying the cheaper Riding mount does not also unlock the armored War mount.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=28915",
        difficultyReason = "Obtain Halaa tokens through contested PvP or an unpredictable garrison mission, then control Halaa to buy the mount.",
        difficulty = "hard",
    },
    [36702] = {
        source = "Attumen the Huntsman - original Karazhan raid, stables",
        category = "Dungeon and Raids",
        faction = "all",
        npcId = 16152,
        requirements = "An eligible character capable of clearing the original Karazhan raid encounter.",
        cost = "No purchase cost for the raid-drop route.",
        tips = "This is the original raid's weekly attempt, not the Legion dungeon's lockout. Different characters provide additional independent chances, not a guaranteed drop after a particular number of kills. The mapped instance floor is the original Karazhan floor.",
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 42, x = 0.469, y = 0.748, step = 1, label = "Original Karazhan - ground-level raid entrance" },
            {
                mapID = 350,
                x = 0.452,
                y = 0.826,
                step = 2,
                label = "Stables - clear the approach to Midnight / Attumen",
                mapName = "Karazhan (original raid): Servant's Quarters",
            },
            {
                mapID = 350,
                x = 0.452,
                y = 0.826,
                step = 3,
                label = "Attumen - defeat and loot the mount boss",
                mapName = "Karazhan (original raid): Servant's Quarters",
            },
        },
        itemId = 30480,
        name = "Fiery Warhorse",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A rare boss drop and daily or weekly loot lockouts make the number of attempts unpredictable.\n\n1. Travel to Karazhan in Deadwind Pass and enter the ORIGINAL raid through the ground-level gatehouse at 46.9, 74.8. Do not enter the raised Legion Return to Karazhan dungeon portal: that instance has a different Attumen and a different mount.\n\n2. Stay on the entry floor and follow the stables corridor toward Midnight and Attumen, around 45.2, 82.6 on the original Servant's Quarters map. Clear the spectral horses and stable hands along the way so their fears and stuns do not drag extra packs into the encounter. You do not need to complete the rest of the tower.\n\n3. Attack Midnight to begin the encounter, defeat Attumen when he joins, and loot Attumen's corpse for a chance at Fiery Warhorse's Reins. Check the body even if you defeated the encounter almost instantly on a high-level character.\n\n4. If the reins do not drop, return after the weekly raid reset or make another attempt on a different eligible character. Reset All Instances does not refresh this character's boss loot. No old Karazhan attunement or Master's Key quest is required for this run.\n\n5. Use Fiery Warhorse's Reins from your bags to learn Fiery Warhorse. This is a ground mount; it does not fly like the Headless Horseman's mount or share the collection entry of Midnight's Eternal Reins.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=30480",
        difficultyReason = "A rare boss drop and daily or weekly loot lockouts make the number of attempts unpredictable.",
        difficulty = "hard",
    },
    [40192] = {
        source = "Kael'thas Sunstrider - The Eye, Tempest Keep",
        category = "Dungeon and Raids",
        faction = "all",
        npcId = 19622,
        requirements = "Flight access to Tempest Keep; an eligible character capable of clearing the original raid encounter.",
        cost = "No purchase cost for the raid-drop route.",
        tips = "The existing weekly farming advice is retained, but a full raid clear is optional. There is no required number of attempts, special looting order, or need to kill the phoenix boss first. This Kael'thas is different from the dungeon boss in Magisters' Terrace.",
        waypoints = {
            { mapID = 109, x = 0.736, y = 0.637, step = 1, label = "The Eye - central Tempest Keep raid entrance" },
            {
                mapID = 334,
                x = 0.5,
                y = 0.138,
                step = 3,
                label = "Kael'thas - advisors, weapons and boss encounter",
                mapName = "Tempest Keep: The Eye",
            },
            {
                mapID = 334,
                x = 0.5,
                y = 0.138,
                step = 4,
                label = "Kael'thas - loot Ashes of Al'ar",
                mapName = "Tempest Keep: The Eye",
            },
        },
        itemId = 32458,
        name = "Ashes of Al'ar",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Hard - A rare boss drop and daily or weekly loot lockouts make the number of attempts unpredictable.\n\n1. Fly to Tempest Keep in eastern Netherstorm. Enter The Eye through the large central floating structure at 73.6, 63.7. The smaller surrounding structures are The Botanica, The Mechanar and The Arcatraz; their bosses do not drop Ashes of Al'ar.\n\n2. Inside, cross Al'ar's central hall and take either outer corridor around toward the northern chamber. Clear any trash blocking your route. You can skip Al'ar, Void Reaver and High Astromancer Solarian; their deaths do not enable or improve the mount drop.\n\n3. Reach Kael'thas Sunstrider in the northern room, around 50.0, 13.8 on The Eye map. Start the encounter and stay inside: kill the four advisors as they activate, then the animated weapons, then the advisors again when they revive. Prioritize Capernian if her crowd control is interrupting your attacks.\n\n4. Defeat Kael'thas when he becomes attackable, waiting through any remaining dialogue or phase transition. On a low-level solo character, dismiss pets if mind control is resetting the fight and return with a stronger character if the encounter is not manageable. Loot Kael'thas himself for the rare Ashes; Al'ar is not the mount's loot source.\n\n5. If it does not drop, try on another eligible character or wait for the weekly raid reset. The Eye has a single original raid difficulty for this purpose; toggling raid size/difficulty or resetting the instance does not create more loot chances for the same saved character.\n\n6. Use Ashes of Al'ar from your bags and confirm it in Collections > Mounts. Learning the mount does not require winning an Arena season or grinding a reputation.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=32458",
        difficultyReason = "A rare boss drop and daily or weekly loot lockouts make the number of attempts unpredictable.",
        difficulty = "hard",
    },
}

